{
 "_what": "Which open-weight models have an MLX build oMLX can load, and their REAL resident size. Replaces two guesses: whether a model is runnable at all (the corpus does not know its format) and how big it is (params x a nominal bytes/param was 27% low on 4-bit).",
 "_why": "Ling-3.0-flash-VL scored 24.6 and was the top candidate for weeks with no MLX build in existence. And _BYTES_PER_PARAM['4bit']=0.55 against a real 0.70 made one estimate miss a measured rate by 48%.",
 "_source": "huggingface_hub.HfApi for availability; `uvx hf-mem --model-id <repo>` for size, read over HTTP Range without downloading weights. Validated against a disk measurement: hf-mem returned 39,803,043,240 B for K2-Horizon-MoVA-36B-A4B-8bit where the local files measure 39.8 GB.",
 "_reproduce": "python3 tools/hf_mlx_scan.py [--refresh]",
 "_retrieved": "2026-10-01",
 "🔴 _limits": [
  "A size is the WEIGHTS only -- no KV cache, no activations, no framework overhead. `hf-mem --experimental` adds KV cache if that is ever needed.",
  "`repo` is the plainest build at the best quantisation we will run. Variant builds (abliterated, DWQ, REAP, OptiQ, msq) are deliberately NOT accepted as 'the MLX build of X' -- a modified copy is a different artifact from the one AA scored.",
  "`repo: null` means not runnable TODAY. mlx-community publishes continuously, so re-run before concluding a model is unavailable.",
  "A null `gb` on a repo that exists means hf-mem could not read it, NOT that the model is small. Never treat it as zero."
 ],
